{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
Oh [G]yonder stands little [F]Maggie,
With her [G]dram glass [D]in her [G]hand.
She's [G]passing by her [F]troubles,
An' a [G]courtin' [D]some other [G]man.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
[G]How can I ever [F]stand it?
For to [G]see those [D]two blue [G]eyes,
They're [G]shinin' like a [F]diamond,
Like a [G]diamond [D]in the [G]skies.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
Now [G]march me down to the [F]station,
With my [G]suitcase [D]in my [G]hand.
I'm goin' [G]away for to leave you, little [F]girl,
I'm goin' [G]to some [D]far distant [G]land.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 4"}
Pretty [G]flowers were made for [F]bloomin',
Pretty [G]stars was [D]made for to [G]shine,
Pretty [G]girls were made for boys to [F]love,
